From 2e97463028ccfa1246033290c968e059d129cf30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anirudh nayak <anirudh.nayak@sandlogic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:30:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [DispatchCreation] Add opt-in data tiling for 2D convolutions

Adds `op_type = conv` encodings for 2D convolutions so a target's encoding
resolver can data-tile them.

- Encoding: CONV_LHS/CONV_RHS/CONV_RESULT operand indices and conv support
  in SerializableAttr::getEncodingProperties.
- AnnotateDataTilingHints: annotate convolutions (channel-mixing, two
  output image dims) when --iree-dispatch-creation-data-tiling-convs is set.
- SetEncoding: when a conv activation is a constant, symmetrically padded
  tensor.pad, encode the unpadded source, drop the kernel offsets from the
  activation map and record the padding and logical input sizes as
  iree_encoding.conv_padding / conv_input_hw / conv_input_c. Inputs without
  encodings (e.g. zero points) are now kept when cloning the op.
- HoistEncodingOps / FuseEncodingOpsIntoDispatchRegions / FusionUtils: allow
  constant tensor.pad in hoisted/fused encoding chains; do not sink
  unset_encoding through transposing consumers.
- DispatchCreation: --iree-dispatch-creation-disable-collapse-dimensions.
- MaterializeEncodingPatterns: fail the match instead of crashing when the
  resolver's lowerOp returns null.
